# Docs and ADRs

Docs and ADRs are part of the change. If you change behaviour, topology, deploy
path, substituters, auth, or a freeze: update the matching `docs/services/` /
runbook / README, and add or amend an ADR under `docs/adr/` (ISO date + slug,
**one decision**).

Do not leave the tree contradicting `docs/standards.md` or the README.

`docs/fleet-audit.md` is an investigation log, not the operational spec. Do
not "fix" it into current truth. Closed coding slips belong in
`docs/todo-deviations.md`; product and topology freezes belong in ADRs.

This is a NixOS flake for a homelab plus two cloud VMs. GitLab is CI of record
(`docs/adr/2026-08-29-gitlab-ci-of-record.md`). Decisions live in
`docs/adr/README.md`. Service docs: `docs/`. Custom options:
`docs/custom-options.md`.
